## Ethics and Morality

### Standard View
- Moral absolutes grounded in God's nature and commands
- Right and wrong defined by divine revelation
- Obedience to God's will as primary moral framework
- Accountability to divine judgment

### Energy-Centered View
- **Ethics grounded in reality's structure**: What actually promotes flourishing vs. destruction
- **Observable consequences**: Actions aligned with energy's patterns sustain complexity; resistance accelerates entropy
- **Interconnection**: "Love your neighbor" recognizes we're all expressions of the same fundamental energy
- **Shalom as systems harmony**: Peace/wholeness occurs when all parts align with their fundamental nature

## The Problem of Evil and Suffering

### Standard View
- Result of the Fall and human sin
- Allowed by God for purposes including free will, character development, or inscrutable divine reasons
- Temporary condition to be resolved in final restoration
- Requires theodicy—defending God's goodness despite evil

### Energy-Centered View
- **Natural consequence of physics**: Entropy, chaos, and destruction are possibilities within any system
- **Conscious agency creates risk**: Beings capable of alignment can also choose misalignment
- **No theodicy needed**: Reality isn't a person whose goodness must be defended; patterns simply operate
- **The challenge**: Developing wisdom to match our power—technical capacity to manipulate energy without understanding of long-term consequences

